0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Motorola 6809
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-23).
0000                             ;  Follows the design of the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two builds, selected by the CHECKED line below (CPM is always 0: the 6809
0000                             ;  has no CP/M; the line is kept only so that build.sh works):
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: an unchecked build checks nothing)
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build: variables start at 0, words start
0000                             ;                 undefined, and every error in the spec's table stops the
0000                             ;                 program with the four-line report, then goes to EXIT:
0000                             ;                   Err X @ line,col
0000                             ;                   <up to 16 characters of the text at the place>
0000                             ;                   Stk n: ... v v v      (n = depth, then the top 8 values)
0000                             ;                   Rtn n
0000                             ;                 S/s data stack over/underflow, R/r return stack over/
0000                             ;                 underflow, H heap, O store outside the program's space,
0000                             ;                 W bad character after [, U undefined word, Q no closing
0000                             ;                 quote, X reserved byte, Z divide by zero, N unbalanced or
0000                             ;                 mismatched brackets, B Ctrl-C.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  A third line, ANSI, says how the four console codes (`@ `^ `_ `?) work:
0000                             ;    ANSI     1 = they send ANSI escape sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = they call four routines of the machine's own instead:
0000                             ;                 CONAT, CONCLS, CONEOL and CONCUR (see the equates)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In both builds Ctrl-C stops a running program (the unchecked build goes
0000                             ;  to EXIT without a word): see the console layer below for the rules, the
0000                             ;  held key and the break-off cell at 827Bh.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, M6809 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; always 0 (no CP/M on the 6809)
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console codes send ANSI sequences
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    Y    IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    U    the data stack pointer. The stack grows down and U points at the
0000                             ;         top cell (TOS); nothing is cached in a register, because every
0000                             ;         dispatch needs A, B and X as scratch. Cells are big-endian here.
0000                             ;         (Only the stacks are big-endian: cells in RAM that the program can
0000                             ;         see - variables, the heap pointer, anything @ and ! reach - are
0000                             ;         little-endian, as the spec says, so @ and ! swap the bytes.)
0000                             ;    S    the return stack. A word call is a plain push of Y. Entries are
0000                             ;         2 bytes, big-endian. Handlers are called with JSR, so the return
0000                             ;         address of the dispatcher is on top of S while a handler runs.
0000                             ;    DP   the letter page, so the letter-page variables below cost 2-byte
0000                             ;         direct addressing. Nothing else may change DP.
0000                             ;    A B X are scratch. Every handler is entered by JSR and ends in RTS (one
0000                             ;    byte). A handler that pushes or pops the return stack first pulls the
0000                             ;    dispatcher's return address into X (PULS X) and ends with JMP ,X.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch (unchecked build). PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character:
0000                             ;  the low byte of the handler's distance from PTAB. The handlers of the last
0000                             ;  characters (in code order) start within 256 bytes after PTAB, the handlers
0000                             ;  of the first NPG1 characters in the 256 bytes after that. The assembler
0000                             ;  works NPG1 out from where five handlers landed, and testing/chktab09.py
0000                             ;  checks the layout. The checked build is bigger than that reach, so its
0000                             ;  table holds whole addresses instead.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM areas:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    8000h-80FFh  return stack (S); empty = 8100h. Unchecked: 127 entries.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 112 entries (S down to 8020h); the 32 bytes below
0000                             ;                 are a guard band for what a handler and an interrupt push
0000                             ;                 on top of a full stack before the check runs.
0000                             ;    8100h-81FFh  data stack (U). Unchecked: 127 cells, empty = 8200h.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 126 cells (U from 81FCh, empty, down to 8100h):
0000                             ;                 the 4 bytes above are a guard band, so a handler that runs
0000                             ;                 on an empty stack writes there and not on the letter
0000                             ;                 cells. A push past the last cell lands on the return
0000                             ;                 stack's bottom entry (80FEh), and the program stops with S
0000                             ;                 before anything reads it.
0000                             ;    8200h-82FFh  letter page (LET): A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h
0000                             ;                 (a word cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the
0000                             ;                 heap pointer at +7Ch (= z10+), interpreter variables in the
0000                             ;                 gaps, and the -n? line buffer at +80h..+FFh. The break-off
0000                             ;                 cell is at +7Bh (827Bh); +7Ah is free.
0000                             ;    8300h-       PROG, the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts
0000                             ;                 after the NUL and grows to HEAPLIM*256 (F000h)
0000                             ;    F000h-       this image (ROM). The reset vector (FFFEh) must point to
0000                             ;                 `start` (see the listing); the image does not contain it.
0000                             ;    FF03h-FF0Bh  the console routines (CONOUT, KEY) and EXIT are supplied
0000                             ;                 by the system and need no space here.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range LET..HEAPLIM*256.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (end the
0000                             ;   routine with TSTA / RTS, or a plain LDA).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   Both are called with JSR. They may change A and CC and must preserve
0000                             ;   B, X, Y, U and DP.
0000                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; ---- with ANSI = 0 the console codes call these (JMP or JSR) ----------------
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF0Ch   ; `@  cursor to the row in X and the column in
                                 ;     D, both from 0
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; `^  clear the screen and home the cursor
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF12h   ; `_  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF15h   ; `?  cursor off if D = 0 (the Z flag is set to
                                 ;     match), on if not
                                 ;   All four may change A, B, X and CC and must preserve Y, U and DP.
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                             ; (the checked startup counts on it being
0000                             ; the page after LETPAGE)
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   20   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ; for your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (direct-page offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   7Ch   ; z10+, the heap pointer (little-endian)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   34h   ; gap after Z: a key held back by the break check
0000                COUNT:    EQU   35h   ; the break check's countdown (1 look in 256)
0000                AT:       EQU   36h   ; checked: the address of the character being
0000                             ;   run (big-endian), the place an error reports
0000                PEND:     EQU   38h   ; checked: the program's end, the first byte
0000                             ;   after its NUL (big-endian): the heap's floor
0000                SSAV:     EQU   3Ah   ; checked: S as each character starts (big-
0000                             ;   endian): the return stack an error reports
0000                SEED:     EQU   76h   ; the random seed (8276h, little-endian): the
0000                             ;   cell whose address `. gives. Nothing sets
0000                             ;   it at the start but the checked build's
0000                             ;   clearing of the page
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   7Bh   ; the break-off cell (827Bh, z9+): 0 = the
0000                             ;   break key is on
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty return stack
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+20h   ; checked: S may go no lower between characters
0000                RSREP:    EQU   RSTOP-16   ; checked: S while the error report runs
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+100h-4*CHECKED   ; empty data stack (a guard if checked)
0000                DSLIM:    EQU   DSPAGE*256   ; checked: U may go no lower between characters
F000                          .ORG   0F000h   
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ;  Startup
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000   10 CE 81 00  START:    LDS   #RSTOP   
F004   CE 82 00               LDU   #DSTOP   
F007   86 82                  LDA   #LETPAGE   
F009   1F 8B                  TFR   A,DP   
F00B                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Zero the whole letter page: every variable starts at 0, every word
                                 ; cell at 0 (undefined: a call stops with U), and so do the
                                 ; interpreter's own cells in the gaps (KEYBUF and the rest). A is
                                 ; still LETPAGE; 256 rounds leave X at the next page, PROG.
                              CLRB      
                              TFR   D,X   
                    SZ:       CLR   ,X+   
                              DECB      
                              BNE   sz   
F00B                          ENDIF      
F00B   10 8E 83 00            LDY   #PROG   ; the reading position
F00F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F00F   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   ; no key held
F011   0F 7B                  CLR   <BRKOFF   ; the break key is on
F013   1F 21                  TFR   Y,X   ; the heap starts after the program's NUL
F015                          ENDIF      
F015   A6 80        SC:       LDA   ,X+   
F017   26 FC                  BNE   sc   
F019   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F01B   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   ; (little-endian)
F01D   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F01F                          IF   CHECKED   
                              STX   <PEND   ; the heap may never go below this
F01F                          ENDIF      
F01F                             ; =============================================================================
F01F                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
F01F                             ; 
F01F                             ;    00h          end of program
F01F                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh       ignored (control, space, DEL)
F01F                             ;    80h-FFh      reserved: ignored, or X in the checked build
F01F                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
F01F                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
F01F                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
F01F                             ;    the rest     punctuation: JSR through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
F01F                             ; =============================================================================
F01F                NEXT:        
F01F                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler:
                                 ; the pointer minus its limit, taken as unsigned, must be no more
                                 ; than the stack's size. Below the limit (an overflow) it wraps to
                                 ; FFxxh, and the compare leaves N set; above the empty point (an
                                 ; underflow) it is just over the size, and N is clear.
                              LEAX   (0-DSLIM)&0FFFFh,U   
                              CMPX   #DSTOP-DSLIM   
                              BHI   e_ds   
                              LEAX   (0-RSLIM)&0FFFFh,S   
                              CMPX   #RSTOP-RSLIM   
                              BHI   e_rs   
                              STY   <AT   ; the place, should this character fail
                              STS   <SSAV   ; and the return stack, as it is now
F01F                          ENDIF      
F01F   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F021   27 50                  BEQ   fin   ; NUL ends the program
F023   80 21                  SUBA   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
F025   25 F8                  BLO   next   ; 01h-20h ignored
F027   81 0F                  CMPA   #0Fh   
F029   25 20                  BLO   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
F02B   81 19                  CMPA   #19h   
F02D   25 2A                  BLO   digit   ; 30h-39h
F02F   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F031   25 16                  BLO   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h: A = 19h-1Fh
F033   80 20                  SUBA   #20h   ; A = c - 41h
F035   81 1A                  CMPA   #1Ah   
F037   25 2C                  BLO   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
F039   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F03B   25 0A                  BLO   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
F03D   81 3A                  CMPA   #3Ah   
F03F   25 1E                  BLO   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
F041   81 3E                  CMPA   #3Eh   
F043                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F043   24 DA                  BHS   next   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
F045                          ENDIF      
F045                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   next   ; 7Fh (DEL): ignored
                              BHI   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
F045                          ENDIF      
F045   80 1A                  SUBA   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
F047   8B 06        P5B:      ADDA   #6   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
F049   80 0A        P3A:      SUBA   #0Ah   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
F04B                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index.
F04B   8E F0 DE     PUNCT:    LDX   #PTAB   
F04E                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F04E                             ; The handler is at PTAB + D, where B is the table byte and A is 1
F04E                             ; for the first NPG1 characters, 0 for the rest.
F04E   E6 86                  LDB   A,X   
F050   81 14                  CMPA   #NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
F052   86 00                  LDA   #0   ; (leaves the carry alone)
F054   49                     ROLA      
F055   AD 8B                  JSR   D,X   ; the handler ends in RTS
F057                          ENDIF      
F057                          IF   CHECKED   
                              ASLA      ; the table holds whole addresses
                              JSR   [A,X]   
F057                          ENDIF      
F057   20 C6                  BRA   next   
F059                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
F059   31 3F        DIGIT:    LEAY   -1,Y   
F05B   8D 27                  BSR   rdnum   
F05D   20 C0                  BRA   next   
F05F                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
F05F   8D 15        LOWER:    BSR   cellx   
F061   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F063   20 BA                  BRA   next   
F065                             ; A-Z: call the word. The IP (the address after the letter) goes on the
F065                             ; return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
F065                             ; Checked: a cell still 0 (high byte 0) was never defined, since every
F065                             ; address in the program's space is 8200h or more. The call has not been
F065                             ; made yet, so the report shows the stacks as they were.
F065   8D 0F        UPPER:    BSR   cellx   
F067   E6 84                  LDB   ,X   
F069   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F06B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   e_undef   
F06B                          ENDIF      
F06B   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F06D   1F 02                  TFR   D,Y   
F06F   8D 31                  BSR   pollk   ; the break check, at every word call
F071   20 AC                  BRA   next   
F073                             ; =============================================================================
F073                             ;  Checked build: the error entries.
F073                             ; 
F073                             ;  Each entry loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside a 3-byte
F073                             ;  CMPX # (the 8Ch), so that a run of them falls through to one place. The
F073                             ;  place an error reports is the address in AT, which the inner loop sets to
F073                             ;  each character before it runs it; the one error that reports another
F073                             ;  place (W, at the character after the [) changes AT before it comes.
F073                             ; 
F073                             ;  The report counts the return stack from SSAV, which the inner loop sets
F073                             ;  to S before each character, so an error may come from any depth of
F073                             ;  calls: a handler, chkst under one, or ctlc under "?" or the break check.
F073                             ;  (An r sets SSAV to the empty stack.) The inner loop's own entries are
F073                             ;  here, where its short branches reach them; those reached from a handler
F073                             ;  are after h_cstore, just ahead of the report.
F073                             ; =============================================================================
F073                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; ---- reached from the inner loop -------------------------------------------
                                 ; The stack checks branch here with N set for an overflow (the pointer is
                                 ; below its limit) and clear for an underflow. After an underflow that stack
                                 ; counts as empty.
                    E_DS:     BMI   e_S   
                              LDU   #DSTOP   ; s
                              LDA   #"s"   
                              BRA   eall   
                    E_RS:     BMI   e_R   
                              LDX   #RSTOP   ; r
                              STX   <SSAV   
                              LDA   #"r"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_S:      LDA   #"S"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_R:      LDA   #"R"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte (80h-FFh) outside a string
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C (from ctlc, at any depth)
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_UNDEF:   LDA   #"U"   ; a word never defined (its cell is still 0)
                    EALL:     JMP   error   
F073                          ENDIF      
F073   7E FF 09     FIN:      JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
F076                             ; cellx: A = letter index (0-25, or 32-57 for lowercase) -> X = cell address
F076   48           CELLX:    ASLA      
F077   8E 82 00               LDX   #LET   
F07A   30 86                  LEAX   A,X   
F07C   39                     RTS      
F07D                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is set if it is a digit
F07D   A6 A4        ISDIG:    LDA   ,Y   
F07F   80 30                  SUBA   #"0"   
F081   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F083   39           AB9:      RTS      
F084                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP and push the value; IP is left on the
F084                             ; first non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says. The running
F084                             ; value lives in the new top cell: V = V*10 + digit.
F084   4F           RDNUM:    CLRA      
F085   5F                     CLRB      
F086   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F088   8D F3        RD1:      BSR   isdig   
F08A   24 F7                  BHS   ab9   
F08C   31 21                  LEAY   1,Y   
F08E   34 02                  PSHS   A   
F090   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F092   58                     ASLB      
F093   49                     ROLA      
F094   58                     ASLB      
F095   49                     ROLA      
F096   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   ; 5V
F098   58                     ASLB      
F099   49                     ROLA      ; 10V
F09A   EB E0                  ADDB   ,S+   
F09C   89 00                  ADCA   #0   
F09E   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F0A0   20 E6                  BRA   rd1   
F0A2                             ; =============================================================================
F0A2                             ;  Console layer: the break key. A running program reads the keyboard only
F0A2                             ;  through pollk and getk, which between them give the break key its rules:
F0A2                             ;    - Ctrl-C (03h) stops the program;
F0A2                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
F0A2                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
F0A2                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
F0A2                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
F0A2                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
F0A2                             ;  On a break the unchecked build ends without a word (EXIT); the checked
F0A2                             ;  one reports B. All three keep B, X, Y and U.
F0A2                             ; =============================================================================
F0A2                             ; pollk: the break check, at every word call and every true ")" loop-back.
F0A2                             ; It looks at the keyboard only once in 256 calls.
F0A2   0A 35        POLLK:    DEC   <COUNT   
F0A4   26 37                  BNE   cc9   
F0A6   BD FF 06               JSR   KEY   
F0A9   27 32                  BEQ   cc9   ; no key
F0AB   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
F0AD   20 0C                  BRA   ctlc   
F0AF                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 with the zero flag set if there is none.
F0AF   96 34        GETK:     LDA   <KEYBUF   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
F0B1   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   ;   the buffer (it has been through ctlc)
F0B3   4D                     TSTA      
F0B4   26 27                  BNE   cc9   
F0B6   BD FF 06               JSR   KEY   
F0B9   27 22                  BEQ   cc9   
F0BB                             ; ctlc: a key has been read. If it is Ctrl-C and the break key is on, that
F0BB                             ; is the end. If the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one
F0BB                             ; more key: a second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the
F0BB                             ; newest wins), and the Ctrl-C goes on: A = 3, zero flag clear.
F0BB   81 03        CTLC:     CMPA   #3   
F0BD   26 1E                  BNE   cc9   
F0BF   0D 7B                  TST   <BRKOFF   
F0C1   27 B0                  BEQ   brk   
F0C3   34 10                  PSHS   X   
F0C5   8E 13 88               LDX   #250*MSLOOP   
F0C8   BD FF 06     CC1:      JSR   KEY   
F0CB   26 06                  BNE   cc2   
F0CD   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F0CF   26 F7                  BNE   cc1   
F0D1   20 06                  BRA   cc3   
F0D3   81 03        CC2:      CMPA   #3   
F0D5   27 9C                  BEQ   brk   
F0D7   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   
F0D9   86 03        CC3:      LDA   #3   
F0DB   35 10                  PULS   X   
F0DD   39           CC9:      RTS      
F0DE                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0DE                BRK:      EQU   fin   ; the unchecked build stops without a word;
F0DE                          ENDIF      
F0DE                          IF   CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B (the report
F0DE                          ENDIF      ;   takes S from SSAV, so the depth of the
F0DE                             ;   calls here doesn't matter)
F0DE                             ; =============================================================================
F0DE                             ;  Dispatch table, in code order.
F0DE                             ; 
F0DE                             ;  Unchecked build: one byte per character, the low byte of the handler's
F0DE                             ;  distance from PTAB. NPG1 is how many characters, from the start, have
F0DE                             ;  handlers more than 255 bytes past PTAB. ] \ [ @ ? sit where the two ranges
F0DE                             ;  meet (in falling code order for this), and which side each lands on is
F0DE                             ;  worked out here. (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it
F0DE                             ;  stores a value.)
F0DE                             ; 
F0DE                             ;  Checked build: it has more code than the two ranges hold, so its table
F0DE                             ;  holds whole addresses and there are no rules about where handlers go.
F0DE                             ; =============================================================================
F0DE                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0DE                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-PTAB)/256   ; 0 = first range, 1 = second
F0DE                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-PTAB)/256   
F0DE                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-PTAB)/256   
F0DE                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-PTAB)/256   
F0DE                PGKEY:    EQU   (h_key-PTAB)/256   
F0DE                NPG1:     EQU   20 + PGKEY + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
F0DE                          ENDIF      
F0DE                PTAB:        
F0DE                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0DE   90                     FCB   (h_store-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; !
F0DF   0F                     FCB   (h_str-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; "
F0E0   A0                     FCB   (h_num-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; #
F0E1   7C                     FCB   (h_print-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; $
F0E2   69                     FCB   (h_swap-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; %
F0E3   C5                     FCB   (h_and-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; &
F0E4   75                     FCB   (h_emit-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; '
F0E5   05                     FCB   (h_open-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; (
F0E6   27                     FCB   (h_close-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; )
F0E7   33                     FCB   (h_mul-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; *
F0E8   CD                     FCB   (h_add-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; +
F0E9   1F                     FCB   (h_cfetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ,
F0EA   D4                     FCB   (h_sub-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; -
F0EB   97                     FCB   (h_cstore-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; .
F0EC   DF                     FCB   (h_div-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; /
F0ED   70                     FCB   (h_dup-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; :
F0EE   79                     FCB   (h_drop-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ;
F0EF   51                     FCB   (h_lt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; <
F0F0   5D                     FCB   (h_eq-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; =
F0F1   4F                     FCB   (h_gt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; >
F0F2   E2                     FCB   (h_key-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ?
F0F3   DC                     FCB   (h_fetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; @
F0F4   A1                     FCB   (h_def-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; [
F0F5   94                     FCB   (h_break-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; \
F0F6   90                     FCB   (h_ret-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ]
F0F7   28                     FCB   (h_xor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ^
F0F8   44                     FCB   (h_alloc-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; _
F0F9   53                     FCB   (h_grave-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; `
F0FA   36                     FCB   (h_tor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; {
F0FB   20                     FCB   (h_or-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; |
F0FC   3E                     FCB   (h_fromr-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; }
F0FD   31                     FCB   (h_not-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ~
F0FE                          ENDIF      
F0FE                          IF   CHECKED   
                              FDB   h_store   ; !
                              FDB   h_str   ; "
                              FDB   h_num   ; #
                              FDB   h_print   ; $
                              FDB   h_swap   ; %
                              FDB   h_and   ; &
                              FDB   h_emit   ; '
                              FDB   h_open   ; (
                              FDB   h_close   ; )
                              FDB   h_mul   ; *
                              FDB   h_add   ; +
                              FDB   h_cfetch   ; ,
                              FDB   h_sub   ; -
                              FDB   h_cstore   ; .
                              FDB   h_div   ; /
                              FDB   h_dup   ; :
                              FDB   h_drop   ; ;
                              FDB   h_lt   ; <
                              FDB   h_eq   ; =
                              FDB   h_gt   ; >
                              FDB   h_key   ; ?
                              FDB   h_fetch   ; @
                              FDB   h_def   ; [
                              FDB   h_break   ; \
                              FDB   h_ret   ; ]
                              FDB   h_xor   ; ^
                              FDB   h_alloc   ; _
                              FDB   h_grave   ; `
                              FDB   h_tor   ; {
                              FDB   h_or   ; |
                              FDB   h_fromr   ; }
                              FDB   h_not   ; ~
F0FE                          ENDIF      
F0FE                PTABEND:      
F0FE                             ; =============================================================================
F0FE                             ;  Handlers that must start in the first range (within 255 bytes of PTAB)
F0FE                             ;  in the unchecked build: ^ _ ` 00bbIHwg ~
F0FE                             ; =============================================================================
F0FE   EC C1        H_OR:     LDD   ,U++   
F100   AA C4                  ORA   ,U   
F102   EA 41                  ORB   1,U   
F104   20 06                  BRA   st0   
F106   EC C1        H_XOR:    LDD   ,U++   
F108   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F10A   E8 41                  EORB   1,U   
F10C   ED C4        ST0:      STD   ,U   
F10E   39                     RTS      
F10F   63 C4        H_NOT:    COM   ,U   
F111   63 41                  COM   1,U   
F113   39                     RTS      
F114                             ; "{" ( n -- ) R: ( -- n )     The dispatcher's return address comes off the
F114                             ; return stack first (PULS X) and is jumped to at the end.
F114   35 10        H_TOR:    PULS   X   
F116   37 06                  PULU   D   
F118   34 06                  PSHS   D   
F11A   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F11C                             ; "}" ( -- n ) R: ( n -- )    The dispatcher's return address comes off
F11C                             ; into D and the entry under it into X; D is then jumped to.
F11C   35 16        H_FROMR:   PULS   D,X   
F11E   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F120   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   
F122                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n (signed: a 16-bit add);
F122                             ; TOS is the old pointer.
F122                             ; Checked: the new top must be at least the program's end (PEND) and below
F122                             ; the limit page. That also catches an add that wraps: the top is always
F122                             ; 8301h-EFFFh and n is -32768..32767, so a sum that carries past FFFFh
F122                             ; lands below 7000h, and one that borrows can't happen.
F122   D6 7C        H_ALLOC:   LDB   <HEAP   
F124   96 7D                  LDA   <HEAP+1   
F126   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   ; the old pointer
F128   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F12A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CMPD   <PEND   
                              BLO   ah9   ; below the program's end
                              CMPA   #HEAPLIM   
                              BLO   ah1   ; the new top must stay below the limit page
                    AH9:      LDA   #"H"   
                              BRA   ejmp   ; (with [ below)
                    AH1:         
F12A                          ENDIF      
F12A   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   
F12C   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F12E   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F130   39                     RTS      
F131                             ; ---- the grave -------------------------------------------------------------
F131                             ; The grave is a prefix: with the character after it, it is one command.
F131                             ; GTAB holds each character with the place of its handler, as a byte to add
F131                             ; to gbase (the handlers are at the end of the image). A handler starts with
F131                             ; A = the character, is entered by the dispatcher's own JSR and ends in RTS.
F131                             ; A character that is not in the table is unsafe: the unchecked build
F131                             ; searches on through memory, the checked build stops with W.
F131                H_GRAVE:      
F131                          IF   CHECKED   
                              STY   <AT   ; the place of anything that goes wrong in
F131                          ENDIF      ;   one of these is the character after the grave
F131   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F133   8E F1 54               LDX   #GTAB   
F136   A1 81        GR1:      CMPA   ,X++   
F138                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F138   26 FC                  BNE   gr1   
F13A                          ENDIF      
F13A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   gr2   
                              TST   ,X   ; 0 ends the table
                              BNE   gr1   
                              LDA   #"W"   
                              JMP   error   
                    GR2:         
F13A                          ENDIF      
F13A   E6 1F                  LDB   -1,X   
F13C   8E F3 1A               LDX   #gbase   
F13F   3A                     ABX      
F140   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F142                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
F142                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
F142                             ; return with the carry clear.
F142   BD F0 7D     HEXC:     JSR   isdig   
F145   25 0A                  BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
F147   84 DF                  ANDA   #0DFh   
F149   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   
F14B   81 06                  CMPA   #6   
F14D   24 04                  BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
F14F   80 F6                  SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
F151   31 21        HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
F153   39           HV9:      RTS      
F154                             ; The table: a character, then its handler's distance from gbase.
F154   21 76        GTAB:     FCB   "!",g_exec-gbase   
F156   24 58                  FCB   "$",g_hex-gbase   
F158   27 50                  FCB   27h,g_nl-gbase   
F15A   2B 24                  FCB   "+",g_inc-gbase   
F15C   2C 00                  FCB   ",",g_rnd-gbase   
F15E   2D 24                  FCB   "-",g_inc-gbase   
F160   2E 37                  FCB   ".",g_seed-gbase   
F162   3C 43                  FCB   "<",g_min-gbase   
F164   3E 3D                  FCB   ">",g_max-gbase   
F166   3F 89                  FCB   "?",g_cur-gbase   
F168   40 AB                  FCB   "@",g_at-gbase   
F16A   5E 78                  FCB   "^",g_cls-gbase   
F16C   5F 81                  FCB   "_",g_eol-gbase   
F16E                          IF   CHECKED   
                              FCB   0   ; the end
F16E                          ENDIF      
F16E                             ; (hexc and the table are here, in the first range, because the layout of
F16E                             ; the unchecked build needs these bytes ahead of the handlers that follow.)
F16E                             ; ---- where the two ranges meet ---------------------------------------------
F16E                             ; The first range ends somewhere among the next five handlers, ] \ [ @ ?
F16E                             ; (they are in falling code order for this): NPG1 follows. Every handler
F16E                             ; below them must start in the second range, and every one above in the
F16E                             ; first.
F16E                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. (PULS X,Y: the dispatcher's
F16E                             ; return address into X, then the saved IP into Y.)
F16E   35 30        H_RET:    PULS   X,Y   
F170   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F172                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
F172                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
F172   EC C1        H_BREAK:   LDD   ,U++   
F174   27 40                  BEQ   sk9   ; false: nothing to do
F176   8D 1F                  BSR   skip   
F178   4D                     TSTA      ; skip returns 0 for ")"
F179                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBMI   fin   ; (and FFh for the NUL: the program ends)
F179                          ENDIF      
F179   26 F3                  BNE   h_ret   
F17B   35 16        RDROP:    PULS   D,X   ; the return address and the block start
F17D   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   ; back to the dispatcher
F17F                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
F17F                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
F17F                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
F17F                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
F17F                             ; checked build stops on it.)
F17F                          IF   CHECKED   
                    DEF1:     CMPA   #" "-"A"+256   
                              BEQ   def2   
                              LEAY   -1,Y   ; anything but a letter or a space: W. The
                              STY   <AT   ;   place is that character, just read
                              LDA   #"W"   
                    EJMP:     JMP   error   ; (H and N come here too)
F17F                          ENDIF      
F17F   A6 A0        H_DEF:    LDA   ,Y+   
F181   80 41                  SUBA   #"A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
F183   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ;   lands 64 bytes up
F185   C4 DF                  ANDB   #0DFh   ; fold case
F187   C1 1A                  CMPB   #26   
F189                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F189   24 0A                  BHS   def2   ; not a letter
F18B                          ENDIF      
F18B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BHS   def1   
F18B                          ENDIF      
F18B   BD F0 76               JSR   cellx   
F18E   1F 20                  TFR   Y,D   
F190   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; little-endian
F192   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F194   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the PSHU)
F195   36 20        DEF2:     PSHU   Y   ; an anonymous block: push its address
F197                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F197                             ; fall into skip
F197                          ENDIF      
F197                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Checked: the skip must end at a "]" (A = 2), or for a false "(",
                                 ; which comes to opf, at a ")" (A = 0). Anything else stops with N.
                              BSR   skip   
                              SUBA   #2   
                              FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the BSR)
                    OPF:      BSR   skip   
                              TSTA      
                              BEQ   sk9   ; (an RTS)
                              LDA   #"N"   
                              BRA   ejmp   
F197                          ENDIF      
F197                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
F197                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
F197                             ; strings are stepped over whole. B counts the open levels.
F197                             ; Unchecked: a NUL first ends the program (for "\" with no closer; anything
F197                             ; else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets anyway).
F197                             ; Checked: a NUL, or a string that runs into it, returns A = FFh, and the
F197                             ; caller decides: "\" ends the program, "(" and "[" stop with N, as they do
F197                             ; for a closer of the other kind. The place is the opener, still in AT.
F197   5F           SKIP:     CLRB      
F198   A6 A0        SK1:      LDA   ,Y+   
F19A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F19A   10 27 FE D5            LBEQ   fin   
F19E                          ENDIF      
F19E                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   ssn   ; A = FFh
F19E                          ENDIF      
F19E   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F1A0   26 02                  BNE   sk2   
F1A2   8D 4E                  BSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
F1A4                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BCS   sk9   ; (or FFh, with the carry set: unclosed)
F1A4                          ENDIF      
F1A4   80 28        SK2:      SUBA   #"("   
F1A6   27 0F                  BEQ   sk3   
F1A8   4A                     DECA      ; ")"
F1A9   27 08                  BEQ   sk4   
F1AB   80 32                  SUBA   #"["-")"   
F1AD   27 08                  BEQ   sk3   
F1AF   81 02                  CMPA   #"]"-"["   
F1B1   26 E5                  BNE   sk1   
F1B3   5A           SK4:      DECB      
F1B4   2A E2                  BPL   sk1   
F1B6   39           SK9:      RTS      ; the closer at this level
F1B7   5C           SK3:      INCB      
F1B8   20 DE                  BRA   sk1   
F1BA                             ; 22h, checked build (the unchecked one is with the handlers below).
F1BA                             ; Checked: a NUL ends the string too, even right after a "/"; skipstr then
F1BA                             ; returns A = FFh with the carry set (the carry is clear at the quote), and
F1BA                             ; """ stops with Q, the string's address already pushed. (skip comes here
F1BA                             ; for its own NUL as well.)
F1BA                          IF   CHECKED   
                    H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
                              BSR   skipstr   
                              LBCS   e_quote   
                              RTS      
                    SS0:      LDA   ,Y+   ; the character after the "/"
                              BEQ   ssn   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
                              BEQ   ssn   
                              CMPA   #"/"   
                              BEQ   ss0   
                              CMPA   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              RTS      ; the quote: C = 0
                    SSN:      SUBA   #1   ; the NUL: A = FFh, C = 1
                              RTS      
F1BA                          ENDIF      
F1BA   AE C4        H_FETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; "@" (the cell in memory is little-endian)
F1BC   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F1BE   20 40                  BRA   cf1   
F1C0                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
F1C0                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
F1C0                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
F1C0                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
F1C0                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
F1C0   AE C4        H_KEY:    LDX   ,U   
F1C2   10 2B 02 19            LBMI   line   
F1C6   C6 14        KT1:      LDB   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
F1C8   BD F0 AF     KT2:      JSR   getk   
F1CB   26 11                  BNE   kt3   
F1CD   5A                     DECB      
F1CE   26 F8                  BNE   kt2   
F1D0   0C 76                  INC   <SEED   ; a millisecond with no key stirs the random
F1D2   26 02                  BNE   kt4   ;   seed by one: how long a key takes to come
F1D4   0C 77                  INC   <SEED+1   ;   is the one thing here that is not the
F1D6                KT4:         ;   same every time
F1D6   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F1D8   26 EC                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
F1DA   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   ; 0?: the countdown from 0 took 65536 ms;
F1DC   27 E8                  BEQ   kt1   ;   run it again, until a key comes
F1DE   6F C4        KT3:      CLR   ,U   
F1E0   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F1E2   39                     RTS      
F1E3                             ; (The line reader, `line`, is at the end of the image: there is no room for
F1E3                             ; it here, between the short branches.)
F1E3                             ; =============================================================================
F1E3                             ;  Handlers that must start in the second range (unchecked build).
F1E3                             ; =============================================================================
F1E3                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
F1E3                             ; the matching ")".
F1E3   EC C1        H_OPEN:   LDD   ,U++   
F1E5                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F1E5   27 B0                  BEQ   skip   ; tail call: skip ends in RTS
F1E7                          ENDIF      
F1E7                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBEQ   opf   ; checked: skip, and check the closer
F1E7                          ENDIF      
F1E7   35 10                  PULS   X   
F1E9   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F1EB   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F1ED                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
F1ED                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
F1ED                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h. (The checked
F1ED                             ; build's is after skip.)
F1ED                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F1ED   36 20        H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
F1EF   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAY)
F1F0   31 21        SS0:      LEAY   1,Y   
F1F2   A6 A0        SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
F1F4   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F1F6   27 F8                  BEQ   ss0   
F1F8   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F1FA   26 F6                  BNE   skipstr   
F1FC   39                     RTS      
F1FD                          ENDIF      
F1FD   AE C4        H_CFETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; ","
F1FF   4F                     CLRA      
F200   E6 84        CF1:      LDB   ,X   
F202   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F204   39                     RTS      
F205                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
F205                             ; drops it and carries on.
F205   EC C1        H_CLOSE:   LDD   ,U++   
F207   10 27 FF 70            LBEQ   rdrop   
F20B   10 AE 62               LDY   2,S   ; the block start, under the return address
F20E   7E F0 A2               JMP   pollk   ; the break check, at every loop-back
F211                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
F211                             ; "*": three 8x8 multiplies; only the low 16 bits are kept.
F211                             ; a = ah:al at 2,U.  b = bh:bl at ,U.
F211   A6 43        H_MUL:    LDA   3,U   
F213   E6 C4                  LDB   ,U   
F215   3D                     MUL      ; al*bh
F216   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; (bh is no longer needed)
F218   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F21A   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F21C   3D                     MUL      ; ah*bl
F21D   EB C4                  ADDB   ,U   
F21F   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; the cross terms, low byte
F221   A6 43                  LDA   3,U   
F223   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F225   3D                     MUL      ; al*bl
F226   AB C4                  ADDA   ,U   
F228   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F22A   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F22C   39                     RTS      
F22D                             ; Signed compares: a-b, then a branch to put -1 or 0 on the stack.
F22D   8D 18        H_GT:     BSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
F22F   8D 10        H_LT:     BSR   cmp   
F231   2D 02                  BLT   true   
F233   5F           FALSE:    CLRB      
F234   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDB)
F235   C6 FF        TRUE:     LDB   #0FFh   
F237   1D                     SEX      ; D = 0000 or FFFF
F238   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F23A   39                     RTS      
F23B   8D 04        H_EQ:     BSR   cmp   
F23D   27 F6                  BEQ   true   
F23F   20 F2                  BRA   false   
F241   EC 42        CMP:      LDD   2,U   
F243   10 A3 C1               CMPD   ,U++   
F246   39                     RTS      
F247                             ; ---- stack, and printing ----------------------------------------------------
F247   37 16        H_SWAP:   PULU   D,X   ; "%"
F249   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F24B   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F24D   39                     RTS      
F24E   EC C4        H_DUP:    LDD   ,U   ; ":"
F250   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F252   39                     RTS      
F253   A6 41        H_EMIT:   LDA   1,U   ; "'"
F255                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F255   8D 49                  BSR   putc   
F257                          ENDIF      
F257                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JSR   CONOUT   ; (the checked build's report is in the way)
F257                          ENDIF      
F257   33 42        H_DROP:   LEAU   2,U   ; ";"
F259   39                     RTS      
F25A                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
F25A                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
F25A                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
F25A                             ; Checked: a NUL (not one escaped by "/") stops with Q, the string's address
F25A                             ; still on the stack.
F25A   AE C4        H_PRINT:   LDX   ,U   
F25C   A6 80        PR0:      LDA   ,X+   
F25E                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBEQ   e_quote   
F25E                          ENDIF      
F25E   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F260   27 F5                  BEQ   h_drop   
F262   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F264   26 04                  BNE   pr1   
F266   A6 80                  LDA   ,X+   
F268   84 BF                  ANDA   #0BFh   
F26A                PR1:         
F26A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F26A   8D 34                  BSR   putc   
F26C                          ENDIF      
F26C                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
F26C                          ENDIF      
F26C   20 EE                  BRA   pr0   
F26E                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." with the high byte stored first. The cell in
F26E                             ; memory is little-endian.
F26E                             ; Checked: both bytes must be in the program's space, and they are tested
F26E                             ; before either is stored (chkst stops with O, the stack untouched).
F26E   AE C4        H_STORE:   LDX   ,U   
F270                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F270   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F272   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F274                          ENDIF      
F274                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BSR   chkst   
                              LEAX   1,X   
                              BSR   chkst   
                              LDA   2,U   
                              STA   ,X   
                                 ; and fall into ".", which loads X again (and checks it again)
F274                          ENDIF      
F274                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F274   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDX)
F275                          ENDIF      
F275   AE C4        H_CSTORE:   LDX   ,U   ; "." ( c addr -- )
F277                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BSR   chkst   
F277                          ENDIF      
F277   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F279   37 06                  PULU   D   
F27B   E7 84                  STB   ,X   
F27D   39                     RTS      
F27E                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; ---- reached from a handler ------------------------------------------------
                                 ; chkst: stop with O unless X is in the program's own space: from the letter
                                 ; page up to HEAPLIM, so the interpreter's stacks and whatever lies above the
                                 ; limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but below the limit is the
                                 ; program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there. Keeps every register.
                    CHKST:    CMPX   #LET   
                              BLO   cs9   
                              CMPX   #HEAPLIM*256   
                              BHS   cs9   
                              RTS      ; in range
                    CS9:      LDA   #"O"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; / by zero
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; " or $ ran into the NUL
                                 ; and fall into error. (H, W and N have their own entries, near
                                 ; their handlers, at ejmp.)
                                 ; =============================================================================
                                 ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
                                 ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
                                 ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
                                 ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
                                 ;  short calls. Prints
                                 ; 
                                 ;     CR LF
                                 ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
                                 ;     <up to 16 raw characters from the place, ending early at CR, LF, NUL>
                                 ;     CR LF
                                 ;     Stk n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
                                 ;     Rtn n CR LF
                                 ; 
                                 ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
                                 ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
                                 ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
                                 ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
                                 ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
                                 ; 
                                 ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 80FEh): the
                                 ;  report's own cells then reach 8 bytes further down, to 80F6h, into the
                                 ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
                                 ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
                                 ; =============================================================================
                    ERROR:    LDS   #RSREP   
                              TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
                              TFR   B,A   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   " @"," "+80h   
                                 ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
                                 ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
                              LDY   #0   
                              LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
                              PSHU   X   
                              LDX   #PROG-1   
                              CMPX   <AT   
                              BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
                              STX   ,U   
                    LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
                    LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
                              CMPX   <AT   
                              BHS   lc3   
                              LDA   ,X   
                              CMPA   #10   
                              BNE   lc2   
                              STX   ,U   
                              BRA   lc1   
                                 ; pmsg: print the text after the call, up to and including the character
                                 ; that has bit 7 set (it is printed without it), then return after it.
                                 ; (It sits here, in the middle of the report, where all its calls reach.)
                    PMSG:     PULS   X   
                    PM1:      LDA   ,X   
                              ANDA   #7Fh   
                              JSR   putc   
                              TST   ,X+   
                              BPL   pm1   
                              JMP   ,X   
                    LC3:      LDD   <AT   
                              SUBD   ,U   
                              STD   ,U   ; the column
                              PSHU   Y   
                              JSR   pdec   ; the line
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   ","+80h   
                              BSR   pdec   ; the column
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10+80h   
                                 ; the text at the place
                              LDX   <AT   
                              LDB   #16   
                    TX1:      LDA   ,X+   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              CMPA   #10   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              CMPA   #13   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              BSR   putc   
                              DECB      
                              BNE   tx1   
                    TX9:      BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
                                 ; the data stack: its depth, then its top 8 cells, from Y down to
                                 ; the program's top cell, at ,U.
                              PSHS   U   ; where the walk ends
                              LDD   #DSTOP   
                              SUBD   ,S   
                              BSR   pdh   ; the depth (pdec leaves U as it was)
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   ":"+80h   
                              LEAY   16,U   ; past the 8th cell from the top ...
                              CMPY   #DSTOP   
                              BHS   sl1   
                              BSR   pmsg   ; (there are more than 8)
                              FCB   " ..","."+80h   
                              BRA   sl2   
                    SL1:      LDY   #DSTOP   ; ... or the whole stack, if no more than 8
                    SL2:      CMPY   ,S   
                              BLS   sl9   
                              LDD   ,--Y   
                              PSHU   D   
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   " "+80h   
                              BSR   h_num   
                              BRA   sl2   
                    SL9:      BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
                              LDD   #RSTOP   ; the return stack's depth, (RSTOP - S) / 2,
                              SUBD   <SSAV   ;   S as it was when this character began
                              BSR   pdh   
                              JSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10+80h   
                              JMP   EXIT   
                                 ; pdh: print D/2 (a depth: D is twice it), unsigned.
                    PDH:      LSRA      
                              RORB      
                              PSHU   D   
                              BRA   pdec   
F27E                          ENDIF      
F27E                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
F27E   6D C4        H_NUM:    TST   ,U   
F280   2A 06                  BPL   pdec   
F282   86 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
F284   8D 1A                  BSR   putc   
F286   8D 58                  BSR   negt   
F288                             ; pdec: print the top cell as unsigned and drop it, by recursion on /10
F288   CC 00 0A     PDEC:     LDD   #10   
F28B   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F28D   8D 62                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = quotient, TOS = digit
F28F   37 06                  PULU   D   ; the digit
F291   34 04                  PSHS   B   
F293   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F295   27 03                  BEQ   pd1   
F297   8D EF                  BSR   pdec   ; (it drops the quotient)
F299   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAU)
F29A   33 42        PD1:      LEAU   2,U   ; drop the zero quotient
F29C   35 02                  PULS   A   
F29E   8B 30                  ADDA   #"0"   ; and fall into putc
F2A0   7E FF 03     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   
F2A3                             ; ---- more arithmetic ---------------------------------------------------------
F2A3   EC C1        H_AND:    LDD   ,U++   
F2A5   A4 C4                  ANDA   ,U   
F2A7   E4 41                  ANDB   1,U   
F2A9   20 04                  BRA   st   
F2AB   EC C1        H_ADD:    LDD   ,U++   
F2AD   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F2AF   ED C4        ST:       STD   ,U   
F2B1   39                     RTS      
F2B2                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
F2B2   BD F0 7D     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
F2B5   25 26                  BLO   negnum   
F2B7   EC 42                  LDD   2,U   
F2B9   A3 C1                  SUBD   ,U++   
F2BB   20 F2                  BRA   st   
F2BD                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F2BD                             ; "/" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F2BD                             ; second range: the divide itself and the routines after it.
F2BD                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F2BD                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F2BD                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
F2BD                             ; it stops with Z, both operands still on the stack.
F2BD                H_DIV:       
F2BD                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDD   ,U   
                              LBEQ   e_zero   
F2BD                          ENDIF      
F2BD   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F2BF   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a's sign: for r
F2C1   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F2C3   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a xor b: for q
F2C5   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F2C7   8D 22                  BSR   absx   ; |a|
F2C9   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F2CB   8D 1E                  BSR   absx   ; |b|
F2CD   8D 22                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = q, TOS = r
F2CF   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F2D1   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F2D3   2A 02                  BPL   dv1   
F2D5   8D 0B                  BSR   negx   ; q's sign
F2D7   6D E0        DV1:      TST   ,S+   
F2D9   2A 0F                  BPL   ng9   
F2DB   20 03                  BRA   negt   ; r's sign
F2DD   BD F0 84     NEGNUM:   JSR   rdnum   ; a negative literal: read it, then negate
F2E0   1F 31        NEGT:     TFR   U,X   
F2E2   EC 84        NEGX:     LDD   ,X   ; negx: negate the cell at X
F2E4   40                     NEGA      
F2E5   50                     NEGB      
F2E6   82 00                  SBCA   #0   
F2E8   ED 84                  STD   ,X   
F2EA   39           NG9:      RTS      
F2EB   6D 84        ABSX:     TST   ,X   ; absx: negate the cell at X if negative
F2ED   2A FB                  BPL   ng9   
F2EF   20 F1                  BRA   negx   
F2F1                             ; udiv: unsigned divide, in place. The dividend is the NOS cell and the
F2F1                             ; divisor the TOS cell, both <= 8000h; the NOS cell becomes the quotient and
F2F1                             ; the TOS cell the remainder. The remainder is built in D (always < the
F2F1                             ; divisor, so 2R+1 fits in 16 bits).
F2F1                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
F2F1   EC C4        UDIV:     LDD   ,U   
F2F3   83 00 02               SUBD   #2   
F2F6   26 07                  BNE   ud0   
F2F8   64 42                  LSR   2,U   
F2FA   66 43                  ROR   3,U   ; the quotient
F2FC   59                     ROLB      ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D was 0)
F2FD   20 18                  BRA   ud3   
F2FF   8E 00 10     UD0:      LDX   #16   
F302   4F                     CLRA      
F303   5F                     CLRB      
F304   68 43        UD1:      ASL   3,U   
F306   69 42                  ROL   2,U   ; the dividend's top bit ...
F308   59                     ROLB      
F309   49                     ROLA      ; ... into the remainder
F30A   10 A3 C4               CMPD   ,U   
F30D   25 04                  BLO   ud2   
F30F   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F311   6C 43                  INC   3,U   ; a quotient bit
F313   30 1F        UD2:      LEAX   -1,X   
F315   26 ED                  BNE   ud1   
F317   ED C4        UD3:      STD   ,U   
F319   39                     RTS      
F31A                             ; =============================================================================
F31A                             ;  The grave's codes (h_grave is the dispatcher). Each is entered with
F31A                             ;  A = the character, and ends in RTS.
F31A                             ; 
F31A                             ;    `!  ( addr -- )        call the machine code at addr. The code is
F31A                             ;                           entered with the address already popped: U
F31A                             ;                           points at the top data cell (big-endian) and the
F31A                             ;                           dispatcher's return address is on top of S. It
F31A                             ;                           may pop and push data cells by changing U; on
F31A                             ;                           return the cell at ,U is the new TOS. It must
F31A                             ;                           keep Y, DP and S (balanced) and return with RTS;
F31A                             ;                           A, B, X and CC may change.
F31A                             ;    `$  ( addr -- addr' )  the hex loader: pairs of hex digits are stored
F31A                             ;                           from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS
F31A                             ;                           (39h) is written and its address is left. An odd
F31A                             ;                           last digit is consumed and dropped.
F31A                             ;    `'  ( -- )             new line: CR LF
F31A                             ;    `+  ( addr -- n )      add 1 to the cell at addr and leave its new value
F31A                             ;    `,  ( n -- r )         a random number from 0 to n-1 (n is 1 to 32767)
F31A                             ;    `-  ( addr -- n )      subtract 1 from the cell at addr, the same way
F31A                             ;    `.  ( -- addr )        the address of the random seed
F31A                             ;    `<  ( a b -- n )       the smaller of the two (signed)
F31A                             ;    `>  ( a b -- n )       the larger
F31A                             ;    `?  ( flag -- )        the cursor off (0) or on
F31A                             ;    `@  ( row col -- )     the cursor to that row and column, both from 0
F31A                             ;    `^  ( -- )             clear the screen and home the cursor
F31A                             ;    `_  ( -- )             clear from the cursor to the end of the line
F31A                             ; 
F31A                             ;  Neither the loader's stores nor the machine code are checked.
F31A                             ; =============================================================================
F31A                GBASE:       
F31A                             ; `, The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes every 16-bit
F31A                             ; value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones and the low
F31A                             ; ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low (EOR) before the
F31A                             ; remainder of dividing by n is taken.
F31A                             ; n must be 1 to 32767: the checked build stops with Z on anything less
F31A                             ; than 1.
F31A                G_RND:       
F31A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDD   ,U   
                              SUBD   #1   ; n - 1 negative: n is 0 or less
                              LBMI   e_zero   
F31A                          ENDIF      
F31A   D6 76                  LDB   <SEED   ; (the cell is little-endian)
F31C   96 77                  LDA   <SEED+1   
F31E   58                     ASLB      
F31F   49                     ROLA      
